tools: say SumatraPDF in usage text, not mutool/mudraw/muraster

SumatraPDF exposes mutool's tools as `SumatraPDF <tool>` subcommands, so the
usage text has to name SumatraPDF and not the mutool / mudraw / muraster
binaries the user never runs. muraster also drops its version banner.

Pure string changes; re-apply by hand if upstream rewords a usage block.
---
diff --git a/source/tools/muconvert.c b/source/tools/muconvert.c
index e290208..cdc755f 100644
--- a/source/tools/muconvert.c
+++ b/source/tools/muconvert.c
@@ -53,7 +53,7 @@ static int count;
 static int usage(void)
 {
 	fprintf(stderr,
-		"Usage: mutool convert [options] file [pages]\n"
+		"Usage: SumatraPDF convert [options] file [pages]\n"
 		"\t-p -\tpassword\n"
 		"\n"
 		"\t-o -\toutput file name (%%d for page number)\n"
